---
import GuideArticle from '../../../../components/GuideArticle.astro';
import { routeOf, brandOf, GUIDE_BASE, routeDetailHref, hasRouteDetail, canonicalRouteSummaryOf } from '../../../../data/phone.js';

const tello = routeOf('tello-paygo-credit-2026')!;
const ultra = routeOf('ultra-mobile-paygo-3-2026')!;
const h2o = routeOf('h2o-paygo-10-90d-2026')!;
const keepOrig = (r: any) => `${r.keep.currency} ${r.keep.yearCostOriginal}`;
const telloCanonical = canonicalRouteSummaryOf('tello-paygo-credit-2026')!;
const conditionalSmsKeep = telloCanonical.metrics.keepYearCostOriginal;
// Standard web checkout is a distinct maintenance method and can cost more.
const ordinaryWebTopupYear = 80;


const guideRouteHref = (r: any) => routeDetailHref(r) || `${GUIDE_BASE}?route=${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}`;
const keepAliveHref = (r: any) => hasRouteDetail(r) ? `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/${r.id}/` : `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/#${r.id}`;
---
<GuideArticle slug="keep-us-number-alive-abroad"
  h1="How to keep a US phone number alive while living abroad"
  title="How to keep a US phone number alive while living abroad (2026)"
  desc="Compare US number retention costs, activation barriers and prepaid SMS evidence. Tello web top-up differs from conditional SMS credit maintenance; first activation abroad is not guaranteed."
  lead="Keeping an existing US number alive is a different job from obtaining and activating a new number from abroad. Compare what each source-backed route actually requires before buying or relying on it for account verification.">

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>The short answer</h2>
<p>If you already have a US-activated number, compare <a href={guideRouteHref(tello)}>{brandOf(tello)?.name} PAYG</a>, <a href={guideRouteHref(ultra)}>{brandOf(ultra)?.name}</a> and <a href={guideRouteHref(h2o)}>{brandOf(h2o)?.name}</a>. Tello PAYG has a documented <strong>conditional SMS top-up path</strong> of about USD {conditionalSmsKeep}/year, while normal web top-ups can require about USD {ordinaryWebTopupYear}/year. These are different maintenance paths; neither is guaranteed to work for every existing account.</p>
<p>Every route below links to its full evidence page, and every retention window has a <a href={keepAliveHref(tello)}>deadline calculator</a> so you never miss the deadline.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Option 1 — Tello PAYG (check eligibility first)</h2>
<p>This is the PAYG credit route, not a $5/month plan. Current canonical evidence requires <strong>first SIM/eSIM activation or port-in on Tello US network towers while physically in the United States</strong> before Wi-Fi Calling or roaming abroad. Do not treat an overseas new-buyer checkout as verified.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Keep-alive rule:</strong> {tello.keep?.action || 'See route page'}</li>
<li><strong>Annual keep cost:</strong> from USD {conditionalSmsKeep}/yr (four $10 SMS top-ups) <em>only when that SMS top-up mechanism is available and the line can send SMS</em>. Standard $20 web PAYG top-ups on a 90-day cycle can instead cost around USD {ordinaryWebTopupYear}/yr. The $5/month plan is a separate product; no price or activation equivalence is inferred.</li>
<li><strong>Abroad:</strong> After US first activation, Wi-Fi Calling &amp; Text or paid international roaming may work where supported; a specific bank/app SMS success is not guaranteed. Some firsthand reports describe outages or failed codes.</li>
<li><strong>Window:</strong> purchase qualifying PAYG credit before the 90-day purchase-expiry window. Ordinary SMS use does not by itself reset that clock; a separate active monthly plan follows different rules.</li>
</ul>
<p>Full evidence and acquisition steps: <a href={guideRouteHref(tello)}>{brandOf(tello)?.name} route page</a>.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Option 2 — Ultra Mobile PayGo</h2>
<p>The famous "$3/month" plan. Officially {keepOrig(ultra)}/yr (≈¥{ultra.keep?.yearCostCny}), 100 minutes + 100 texts + 100MB included monthly.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Abroad:</strong> {ultra.chinaActivation || ''}</li>
<li><strong>Caveat:</strong> PayGo cannot be converted to other Ultra plans, and roaming rates in China are billed per-use ($0.10/SMS received).</li>
</ul>
<p>Full evidence: <a href={guideRouteHref(ultra)}>{brandOf(ultra)?.name} route page</a>.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Option 3 — H2O Wireless pay-as-you-go</h2>
<p>{h2o.acquisitionSummary || 'AT&T-network MVNO with pay-as-you-go credit.'}</p>
<p>Retention evidence is still being verified — check the current status on <a href={guideRouteHref(h2o)}>the H2O route page</a> before committing.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Routes to avoid</h2>
<p>Some US routes look cheap but are dead ends or unverifiable. Anything we could not verify stays out of this guide rather than being guessed. The full <a href={`${GUIDE_BASE}directory/`}>global directory</a> marks every route's evidence status, including the <strong>avoid list</strong>.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Set it and forget it</h2>
<p>Whichever route you pick: open the <a href={keepAliveHref(tello)}>deadline calculator</a>, do the first keep-alive action, record the date, and export the .ics reminder. The calculator uses an earlier reminder only when the evidence packet documents one; otherwise it uses the documented retention window without inventing a buffer.</p></section>
</GuideArticle>
